* two_tone.cir -- FOUR/THD coverage on a signal with known, deliberately-added harmonic content.
*
* v(t) = sin(2*pi*10*t) + 0.1*sin(2*pi*20*t): a 10 Hz fundamental of amplitude 1 plus an exact
* second harmonic of amplitude 0.1 (10% of the fundamental) added on top, so, by hand:
* THD = 100% * sqrt(sum of every harmonic above the fundamental, squared) / fundamental
*     = 100% * 0.1 / 1 = 10% exactly.
* h1_mag should be ~1.0, h2_mag ~0.1, h3_mag (and DC) ~0 -- there is no third harmonic in this
* signal at all.
SIG1 kind=sinwave v0=0 va=1 freq=10
SIG2 kind=sinwave v0=0 va=0.1 freq=20
TOTAL kind=sum inputs=SIG1,SIG2 signs=1,1
VTOT a 0 TOTALV
TOTALV kind=sig2voltage in=TOTAL
R1 a 0 1000

MEAS_FOUR kind=measure type=four out=V(a) fundamental=10 harmonics=4
